  "id": "Compound::DB01232 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Saquinavir is implicated in the pathogenesis of Cyp2c19 through a series of interconnected mechanisms involving anti-infective agents and organonitrogen compounds. The evidence suggests that Saquinavir causes Cytomegalovirus Retinitis and Chorioretinitis, both of which are mediated by Pentamidine, which binds to Cyp2c19. This indicates a potential pathway where Saquinavir indirectly influences Cyp2c19 through the activation of viral infections, which in turn may alter metabolic processes involving Cyp2c19. The presence of Organonitrogen Compounds as common ancestors further supports a broader biological context where these compounds may play a role in drug metabolism or disease pathogenesis. While the direct causal link between Saquinavir and Cyp2c19 remains indirect, the cumulative evidence points to a plausible mechanism involving the interaction of Saquinavir with viral infections, which then modulate Cyp2c19 activity.",
